{{also|płód}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/plɒd/}}, {{SAMPA|/plQd/}}
* {{audio|en-us-plod.ogg|Audio (US)}}
*: {{rhymes|ɒd}}

===Etymology 1===
From  {{etyl|enm}} *{{term||plodden|lang=enm}} (found only in derivative {{term|plodder|lang=enm}}), probably originally a splash through water and mud, from {{term|plod||a puddle|lang=enm}}. Compare {{etyl|da|-}} {{term|pladder||mire|lang=da}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-}}

# A [[slow]] or [[labored]] [[walk]] or other [[motion]] or [[activity]].
#: ''We started at a brisk walk and ended at a '''plod'''.''

====Verb====
{{en-verb|plodd|ing}}

# {{intransitive}} To [[walk]] or [[move]] [[slowly]] and [[heavily]] or [[laboriously]] (+ on, through, over).
# {{transitive}} To [[trudge]] over or through.

* {{seeCites}}

